.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam \- manage Euclid users, groups, accounts, namespaces and access grants
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-loglevel\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
.B eam
.I action
[\fIaction-options\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B eam
module talks to the Euclid gateway's eam service to authenticate and
manage the access-control hierarchy: accounts, the namespaces under them
(e.g. \fIdevelopment\fR, \fIintegration\fR, \fIproduction\fR), users, user
groups, per-user namespace grants, and which namespace the current session
is restricted to. Every
.B eam
command sends a single JSON request to the gateway
(\fB\-\-endpoint\fR, default \fIhttp://localhost:5566\fR) and prints the
JSON response on success.
.PP
Most actions other than
.B login
require the caller to be authenticated; see
.B AUTHENTICATION
below for how the session token is obtained and stored, and
.B ADMINISTRATOR PRIVILEGES
below for how the two levels of administrator access work.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B login
Authenticates with a user ID and password and stores the returned bearer
token for use by later commands. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1).
.TP
.B register
Creates a new user account. Requires administrator privileges, with one
exception: bootstrapping the very first account. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-register (1).
.TP
.B list-users
Lists user accounts, optionally filtered by user ID prefix, paged and
sorted. Requires administrator privileges. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-users (1).
.TP
.B delete-user
Deletes a user account by user ID. Requires administrator privileges. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-user (1).
.TP
.B create-access-key
Creates a new SigV4 access key for the logged-in user and stores it
locally. Self-service; no administrator privileges required. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-access-key (1).
.TP
.B list-access-keys
Lists the logged-in user's own access keys. Self-service; no
administrator privileges required. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-access-keys (1).
.TP
.B delete-access-key
Deletes one of the logged-in user's own access keys. Self-service; no
administrator privileges required. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-access-key (1).
.TP
.B create-user-group
Creates a new, empty user group. Requires administrator privileges. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-user-group (1).
.TP
.B list-user-groups
Lists user groups, optionally filtered by name prefix, paged and sorted.
Requires administrator privileges. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-user-groups (1).
.TP
.B user-group-add-user
Adds a user to a user group. Requires administrator privileges. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-user-group-add-user (1).
.TP
.B user-group-remove-user
Removes a user from a user group. Requires administrator privileges. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-user-group-remove-user (1).
.TP
.B delete-user-group
Deletes a user group by name. Requires administrator privileges. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-user-group (1).
.TP
.B create-account
Creates a new account, the top level of the access hierarchy. Requires
global administrator privileges. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-account (1).
.TP
.B list-accounts
Lists accounts, optionally filtered by account ID prefix, paged and
sorted. Requires global administrator privileges. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-accounts (1).
.TP
.B delete-account
Deletes an account by account ID. The account must have no remaining
namespaces or user grants. Requires global administrator privileges. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-account (1).
.TP
.B create-namespace
Creates a new namespace under an account. Requires administrator
privileges on that account. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-namespace (1).
.TP
.B list-namespaces
Lists the namespaces under an account, optionally filtered by name
prefix, paged and sorted. Requires administrator privileges on that
account. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-namespaces (1).
.TP
.B delete-namespace
Deletes a namespace under an account. The namespace must have no
remaining user grants. Requires administrator privileges on that account.
See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-namespace (1).
.TP
.B grant-namespace-access
Grants a user access to a specific namespace within a specific account.
Requires administrator privileges on that account. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-grant-namespace-access (1).
.TP
.B revoke-namespace-access
Revokes a user's access to a specific namespace within a specific
account. Requires administrator privileges on that account. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-revoke-namespace-access (1).
.TP
.B change-namespace
Switches the active namespace for this session (or clears it), validated
against the caller's own grants. Self-service; no administrator
privileges required beyond having been granted the target namespace. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-change-namespace (1).
.SH ADMINISTRATOR PRIVILEGES
There is no per-user "is admin" field. Instead, two independent levels of
administrator privilege exist:
.TP
.B Global administrator
Membership in the user group named
.IR administrator .
A global administrator may manage every user, user group, account and
namespace in the deployment. Grant or revoke it with
.BR euclid-cli-eam-user-group-add-user (1)
/
.BR euclid-cli-eam-user-group-remove-user (1)
on the
.I administrator
group.
.TP
.B Account-scoped administrator
A per-user, per-account grant (separate from namespace access grants)
that allows managing one account's namespaces and namespace-access grants
without being a global administrator. Account creation and deletion
themselves are always global-administrator-only.
.PP
Account-scoped administrator status cannot currently be granted through
this CLI; it is set when the grant is created programmatically (e.g. the
bootstrap account grant given to the default administrator user).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These options are given to
.B euclid-cli
itself, before the
.I eam
module name.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-endpoint " " \fIURL\fR
Euclid gateway endpoint to talk to, e.g. \fIhttp://localhost:5566\fR. If
omitted, an empty endpoint is used, which will fail to connect.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a JSON configuration file providing defaults for action
options (currently used by
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1)
only). Defaults to
.IR /usr/local/euclid/etc/euclid.json ;
silently ignored if the file doesn't exist.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-signature " " \fISCHEME\fR
Signature scheme used for signed service calls: \fIsigv4\fR (the
default) or \fIrfc9421\fR for RFC 9421 HTTP Message Signatures. Both
prove the request with the same access key; RFC 9421 puts the
signature in \fISignature\fR/\fISignature\-Input\fR headers and binds
the body through \fIContent\-Digest\fR (RFC 9530) instead of using
AWS's Authorization header. Overrides
.I euclid.cli.signature
from the configuration file. Ignored for
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1)
commands, which authenticate with the session's bearer token.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-loglevel " " \fILEVEL\fR
Log level: one of \fItrace\fR, \fIdebug\fR, \fIinfo\fR, \fIwarning\fR,
\fIerror\fR, \fIfatal\fR. Defaults to \fIinfo\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print top-level usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the euclid-cli version and exit.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
.B euclid-cli-eam-login (1)
exchanges a user ID and password for a signed bearer token (a JWT, valid
for one hour by default) and saves it as JSON at
.IR $HOME/.euclid/credentials .
The containing directory is created if needed and both the directory
(\fI0700\fR) and the file (\fI0600\fR) are restricted to the current user,
since the file grants whoever can read it your session.
.PP
Every subsequent
.B eam
command automatically loads this token at startup and sends it as an
.I "Authorization: Bearer"
header. If the server rejects a request with
.I "HTTP 401"
(the token is missing, invalid, or has expired), the stored credentials
file is deleted so that the failure is unambiguous, and you need to run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.PP
The same file also holds the session's active namespace, set via
.B \-\-namespace
on
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)
or via
.BR euclid-cli-eam-change-namespace (1),
and sent as the
.I x\-euclid\-namespace
header on every command afterward, in every module - not just eam. This
is the only way namespace scoping is applied; there is no per-command
override. A session with no namespace set (the default) sends no such
header and behaves exactly as before this mechanism existed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The action completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Argument parsing failed, the request could not be sent, or the server
rejected it (invalid credentials, missing/expired session, insufficient
privileges, invalid input, an account/namespace still in use, etc.).
Details are printed to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.euclid/credentials
JSON file holding the current session's bearer token, created by
.B login
and consumed by every other
.B eam
action.
.SH EXAMPLES
Bootstrap the first administrator account (allowed unauthenticated only
while the user store is empty), then log in:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam register \e
    --region eu-central-1 --account-id 000000000000 \e
    --user admin --email admin@example.com --password 'change-me'

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam login \e
    --user admin --password 'change-me'
.fi
.RE
.PP
List every user, then delete one:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-users

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam delete-user --userId jdoe
.fi
.RE
.PP
Set up a new account with a development namespace, and grant a user
access to it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam create-account \e
    --account-id 123456789012 --name "Payments Team"

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam create-namespace \e
    --account-id 123456789012 --name development

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam grant-namespace-access \e
    --user ern:euclid:eam:eu-central-1:123456789012:user:jdoe \e
    --account-id 123456789012 --namespace development
.fi
.RE
.PP
Make that namespace active for the current session, so subsequent
.B eqs
/
.B ens
/
.B esm
commands are automatically scoped to it without a per-command flag:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam change-namespace \e
    --namespace development
.fi
.RE
